--
--   **Context.** CRT reversal §4: one rotation set and one composite swap in IL
--
--   * `rotIt sig`: one digit-selector rotation (`rotDU`) and the register advance
--     `P_t ← P_t·Q`, `vol C ← vol C / Q`, `D ← D/Q` (`sig`) or `D·Q`, `t ← t+1`.
--   * `lsU sig neg`: the rotation set `L(±σ)` / `L(±1)`: push `Q`, `μ = Q-1` (`neg`) or `1`, and the
--     start values from the global registers, run `m = ⌊n/2⌋` iterations (`rptX` on `rH`), pop.
--     **`lsU_runs`**: the data `xs` (shape `SH n Q T`) becomes `pull … (lsetK Q n m sig μ m) xs`.
--   * `swpU`: the composite Lemma 12 swap of the blocks `x`, `y` (`swS` with `u' = u·m`,
--     `2^{u'} = Q^m`). **`swpU_runs`**: the data becomes `pull … (bsw n m) xs`.
--
--   Global registers (set by the prologue of `p2E`): `gQm = Q^m`, `gP = Q^{n-m}`,
--   `gB = Q^{m-1} · vol T`, `gD = Q^{m-1}`, `gI = n - m`, `gUm = u·m`, `gMd = Q^{n-2m}`; `rH = m`,
--   `rB = vol T / 2`, `oSP` holds `n` copies of `Q`.
